(2322203, 315229, 38549, '<td valign="top">***Greetings from the critique club***<br/>First off i have to say thank you for entering the challenge, that what keeps dpc going.<br/> <br/>ok,...<br/>first of all i like you photo, it seems like you had a great idea, <br/> <br/>things i notice,<br/> <br/>to me it doesnt seem in focus, not that its not in focus, i see the focus point twoards the bottom chalk piece, which leaves the rest kinda not sharp.<br/> <br/>I think a black background would have escentuated the color better, and you could have up the colors thru hue/saturation <br/> <br/>over all i think this is a good photo it would have scored better if the color was more vibrand and it was a little sharper<br/> <br/>Great shot, keep shooting.</td>', '***Greetings from the critique club***First off i have to say thank you for entering the challenge, that what keeps dpc going. ok,...first of all i like you photo, it seems like you had a great idea,  things i notice, to me it doesnt seem in focus, not that its not in focus, i see the focus point twoards the bottom chalk piece, which leaves the rest kinda not sharp. I think a black background would have escentuated the color better, and you could have up the colors thru hue/saturation  over all i think this is a good photo it would have scored better if the color was more vibrand and it was a little sharper Great shot, keep shooting.', '2006-04-18 15:38:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2322481, 316511, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>"Bunny Art" is a nice entry into the Children''s Toy challenge.   I like the idea, having a child''s toy creating something of the real world.  This was a tough category with so many different toys out there to choose from.  <br/> <br/> I think your placement of the subject is good a lillte off center so that everything can be taken in.  Unfortunately the lighting is a bit harsh.   Possibly it was a flash used in a dark environemnet.  You might try using a couple different lights and some reflectors. Even natural light migh balance out the piece a little more even though it usually creates a bunc of shadwos.  Lighting is one of the hardest aspect of photography for myself.   I also like how your focus is on the bunny not the pencils or the art piece.  <br/> <br/>I think you have the idea and creativity and looking at your portfolio you have some great work.   Keep up the good work and I look forward to your future entries.</td>', '*Critique Club* "Bunny Art" is a nice entry into the Children''s Toy challenge.   I like the idea, having a child''s toy creating something of the real world.  This was a tough category with so many different toys out there to choose from.    I think your placement of the subject is good a lillte off center so that everything can be taken in.  Unfortunately the lighting is a bit harsh.   Possibly it was a flash used in a dark environemnet.  You might try using a couple different lights and some reflectors. Even natural light migh balance out the piece a little more even though it usually creates a bunc of shadwos.  Lighting is one of the hardest aspect of photography for myself.   I also like how your focus is on the bunny not the pencils or the art piece.   I think you have the idea and creativity and looking at your portfolio you have some great work.   Keep up the good work and I look forward to your future entries.', '2006-04-18 16:57:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2322593, 316671, 38549, '<td valign="top">***Greetings From the Critique club***<br/>First off i must say thank you for entering the challenge its what makes dpc what it is today<br/> <br/>to start, i must say i like your photograph, it puts a turn on the norm around here.<br/> <br/>you composition is good, the rule of thirds was used, your backgroud coencides with the picture. i really like how the doll is dark and scary and the background is a light normal setting really adds to the photo. <br/>its well focused and shows great texture and detail, perfect dof, you can tell what it is in the backgroudn but it take you a second, i really have nothing to say bad abot the photo, to me it perfect, it should have scored higher, people dont put into thought the time and effort you put into this photo. <br/> <br/>Great job.</td>', '***Greetings From the Critique club***First off i must say thank you for entering the challenge its what makes dpc what it is today to start, i must say i like your photograph, it puts a turn on the norm around here. you composition is good, the rule of thirds was used, your backgroud coencides with the picture. i really like how the doll is dark and scary and the background is a light normal setting really adds to the photo. its well focused and shows great texture and detail, perfect dof, you can tell what it is in the backgroudn but it take you a second, i really have nothing to say bad abot the photo, to me it perfect, it should have scored higher, people dont put into thought the time and effort you put into this photo.  Great job.', '2006-04-18 17:40:11.000000', NULL, 0),
